<h2>The Awakening</h2>
An inky blackness stretches beyond all measure. Boundless. Edgeless. No earth beneath you. No heavens above. Not even the mercy of a grave.

Here, there is no weight to carry. No ache of flesh. No name to answer to.

Yet there is an insistence. Faint, almost imperceptible. Something that ought to have a name. A face. A place among the living.

